  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multisectoral strategy to respond to the urgent needs of the most vulnerable families affected by floods in Tumbes, Piura y Lambayeque</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide nutrition, education , health, child protection and water, sanitation and hygiene (WASH) assistance to vulnerable communities affected by flooding. This UNICEF project provides critical life-saving humanitarian assistance to the most vulnerable families affected by the floods in Tumbes, Piura and Lambayeque.. The project provides humanitarian assistance to 72,000 people, including 25,200 women, 25,200 men, 21,600 children, and including 7,200 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
